1
00:00:06,534 --> 00:00:12,720
Emergency aid often disappears between the donation and the person it should reach.

2
00:00:12,720 --> 00:00:19,264
AidBlink closes that loop: real on-chain funding, and benefits that can't be double-spent.

3
00:00:19,264 --> 00:00:24,658
Step 1 · Contribute. A supporter opens the Blink and connects a wallet.

4
00:00:24,658 --> 00:00:29,308
They pick an amount — here, 0.1 SOL.

5
00:00:29,308 --> 00:00:35,209
Connect Phantom. The wallet signs a real Devnet transaction.

6
00:00:35,209 --> 00:00:41,888
Approve. A genuine on-chain transfer, not a simulation.

7
00:00:41,888 --> 00:00:47,136
Confirmed on-chain. The contribution is now in the aid pool.

8
00:00:47,136 --> 00:00:53,457
The explorer shows the signature, the program and the treasury.

9
00:00:53,457 --> 00:01:01,829
It's a standard Solana Blink — one shareable link any Blink client can render, so donating never requires a new app.

10
00:01:01,829 --> 00:01:07,271
Step 2 · Administer. The organization signs in to manage the pool.

11
00:01:07,271 --> 00:01:11,039
A demo gate with example users.

12
00:01:11,039 --> 00:01:15,706
The dashboard reads the aid pool live from the on-chain ledger.

13
00:01:15,706 --> 00:01:21,099
Record a pseudonymous request — no personal data, just a reference.

14
00:01:21,099 --> 00:01:27,560
Set a small amount and create the request.

15
00:01:27,560 --> 00:01:31,224
It's pending. Approving issues a signed voucher.

16
00:01:31,224 --> 00:01:34,361
Approved — the voucher is issued.

17
00:01:34,361 --> 00:01:38,962
Step 3 · Deliver. The beneficiary gets a QR link.

18
00:01:38,962 --> 00:01:44,406
The QR carries a signed token; single use is enforced server-side.

19
00:01:44,406 --> 00:01:51,325
The partner terminal is a separate role. Sign in as the partner.

20
00:01:51,325 --> 00:01:57,076
The partner verifies the signed token.

21
00:01:57,076 --> 00:02:00,022
Redeemed — the voucher is spent.

22
00:02:00,022 --> 00:02:02,848
Now try the exact same token again.

23
00:02:02,848 --> 00:02:08,336
Rejected. A benefit can only be used once — and the attempt is logged.
